# A conversion out of a box goes by the type of what lies in it: what is no int32 is read as a double, and what is no number is taken for the first marker of the type, unasked. Under a false proof that is silent.
# Under the words on proofs those two arms ask. Here the guard of f1 unboxes its operand for a Body that takes a Double, one record behind its own test: no check in the Body can see what came.
# THE LIE: testing=RowSaysLess:Callee/f1/TestsOfGuard: the emitter lets every test of the guard of f1 pass.
# f1 = sum
# RUN: plan units mechanisms=all
# CHECK: unit f1:Body (Double)
# CHECK: unit f1:ParameterGuard (JSValue) -> (JSValue) tests (number)
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: 40 -1
# RIGHT-NEXT: 0NaNabNaNabNaNabNaNab
# RIGHT-NEXT: went on
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(ENTRIES): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtEntries,RowSaysLess:Callee/f1/TestsOfGuard
